    "question": "**Staleness on watchlist update** — when a watchlist's `terms[]` or `boolean_query` changes, existing match records reflect the old definition. A re-match trigger (e.g. re-running `matchesWatchlist()`/`matchesAst()` over affected posts on UPDATE of `watchlists`) or an explicit per-watchlist reindex endpoint would address this. Deferred; named as a known risk. For `keyword`/`hashtag` watchlists a re-match is straightforward (evaluate `terms[]` against `body_markdown`); for `boolean_query` watchlists it requires running the full AST evaluator, which is available in `social-listening-core`'s `matchesAst()`.",
